WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.401
-Good evening, everybody.
I'm Seth Meyers.

00:00:02.401 --> 00:00:03.636
This is "Late Night."
We hope you're all

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:05.371
doing well tonight and now,
if you don't mind,

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:06.439
we're going to get to the news.

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:08.607
President Biden today signed

00:00:08.607 --> 00:00:10.910
the Respect for Marriage Act
into law.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:13.679
Respecting marriage?
Wow, he really is

00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:15.814
undoing all of Trump's orders.

00:00:15.814 --> 00:00:17.751
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:17.751 --> 00:00:21.120
Los Angeles Mayor Karen Bass
yesterday officially resigned

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:22.388
from the House
of Representatives,

00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:24.990
which means she's the only
person in Los Angeles

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:26.993
who doesn't have
at least two gigs.

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:30.430
"Me? I'm a mayor/
congresswoman/waiter."

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:31.564
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:33.366
When asked yesterday
if he would consider

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:34.634
leaving the Democratic Party,

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:36.736
like Arizona
Senator Kyrsten Sinema,

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:39.072
West Virginia Senator
Joe Manchin told reporters,

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:41.340
"I'll look at all
of these things.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:43.276
I've always looked
at all those things,

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:45.812
but I have no intention
of doing anything right now."

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:48.414
Well, he sounds
like a Democrat to me.

00:00:48.414 --> 00:00:50.316
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:52.819
New York Mayor Eric Adams
spoke today

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:55.522
at the National Mathematics
Improvement Project,

00:00:55.522 --> 00:00:57.823
but this is sad --
he used the opportunity

00:00:57.823 --> 00:00:59.526
to promote division.

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:02.529
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.265 --> 00:01:07.467
Coming around, you guys.

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:08.601
You know what's happening
right now.

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:10.003
You're doing the math
on that joke

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:11.004
and it's working up.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:14.507
It's adding up.
It's adding up.

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:17.277
The New York Times yesterday
released its list

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:20.379
of The 93 Most Stylish 'People'
of 2022.

00:01:20.379 --> 00:01:23.716
Don't bother asking,
Portia from "White Lotus."

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:26.019
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:27.387
Sam Bankman-Fried,

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:30.256
the disgraced founder
of cryptocurrency exchange FTX,

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:31.990
was arrested yesterday
in the Bahamas.

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:33.593
Oh, they got him, huh?

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:36.829
I can't believe he wasn't able
to blend in.

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:38.664
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.664 --> 00:01:40.567
Who fingered him, the humidity?

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:42.335
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:44.837
HBO tonight debuted
"Pelosi in the House,"

00:01:44.837 --> 00:01:46.205
which is a new documentary

00:01:46.205 --> 00:01:47.740
about House Speaker
Nancy Pelosi

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.575
and not, as I had assumed,

00:01:49.575 --> 00:01:51.244
a sitcom on the CW.

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:53.245
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.245 --> 00:01:54.413
According to a new study,

00:01:54.413 --> 00:01:56.449
people who use an alarm clock
to wake up

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:59.452
are more tired than people
who wake up naturally.

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:02.555
Though, people who wake up
naturally tend to be more fired.

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:06.526
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:09.528
A cow in Virginia recently
escaped from a trailer

00:02:09.528 --> 00:02:11.964
and crashed through the glass
doors of an office --

00:02:11.964 --> 00:02:14.067
Oh, sorry,
I read the punch line first.

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:16.201
What's black and white
and red all over?

00:02:16.201 --> 00:02:20.172
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:20.172 --> 00:02:21.241
[ Ohhs ]

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:24.777
Another math joke.

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:27.112
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.112 --> 00:02:29.148
And, finally,
according to new research,

00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:31.417
taking the erectile dysfunction
drug Viagra

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:33.353
can decrease the risk
of developing

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:35.054
Alzheimer's disease,
which is great,

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:36.322
because there's nothing worse

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:38.524
than getting an erection
and forgetting why.

00:02:38.524 --> 00:02:41.894
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:41.894 --> 00:02:44.263
[ Fresh laughter ]

00:02:44.263 --> 00:02:45.598
"Who was here?"

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:46.699
[ Applause ]
-Whoo!

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:48.201
-And that was the monologue,
everybody.

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:49.269
We got a great show
for you tonight.

